# {{project_name}}

An [Autumn](https://crates.io/crates/autumn-web) web application.

## Quickstart

Run these steps top-to-bottom on a clean checkout to get a route serving.

### 1. Prerequisites

- **Rust {{rust_version}}+** (edition 2024) — https://rustup.rs
- **The `autumn` CLI:**
  ```sh
  cargo install autumn-cli --version {{autumn_version}}
  ```
- **The Tailwind binary** (downloaded by `autumn setup`):
  ```sh
  autumn setup
  ```
- **A reachable Postgres** for database features. Don't have one? The golden
  path in step 2 below ("Configure the database") includes a one-line Docker
  option that matches the connection `url` you set there — no need to start a
  container here; just follow that step in order. To generate a full
  deployment/compose stack instead, see
  `autumn release init --target docker-compose` in the CLI reference below.
- **The PostgreSQL client library (`libpq`).** The default scaffold keeps the
  `db` feature, so the base app links `libpq` at build time — it must be
  installed for `cargo build` / `autumn dev` to succeed, even before you have a
  running database configured. It is also required by the Diesel CLI's
  `postgres` feature installed below. Install it with your package manager (e.g.
  `libpq-dev` on Debian/Ubuntu, `libpq` via Homebrew on macOS).
- **Diesel CLI** for the database path (its `postgres` feature needs the
  `libpq` client library above):
  ```sh
  cargo install diesel_cli --no-default-features --features postgres
  ```

### 2. Configure the database

The base scaffold ships with the `[database]` block in `autumn.toml` **commented
out**. `autumn migrate` needs a resolved connection URL, so enable the database
before running it — open `autumn.toml`, uncomment the `[database]` block, and set
`url` to a reachable Postgres:

```toml
[database]
url = "postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/{{crate_name}}"
```

Don't have a Postgres to point at? Start a throwaway local instance with Docker.
This matches the `url` above (user and password `postgres`, database
`{{crate_name}}`), so the two line up with no extra edits. The `-d` flag runs it
in the background so your terminal stays free for the next steps; stop it later
with `docker stop {{crate_name}}-pg`:

```sh
docker run -d --rm --name {{crate_name}}-pg -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres \
  -e POSTGRES_DB={{crate_name}} -p 5432:5432 postgres:16

# Wait until Postgres is ready to accept connections
until docker exec {{crate_name}}-pg pg_isready -U postgres >/dev/null 2>&1; do sleep 1; done
```

The container reports "started" the instant it launches, but first-time Postgres
initialization takes a few seconds before it accepts connections. `autumn db
create` connects immediately and does not retry, so wait for the readiness loop
above to finish before running it.

Then create the database on its server (idempotent — safe to re-run; harmless if
the container above already created it):

```sh
autumn db create
```

> Need containerized **deployment** assets (a production Dockerfile plus a
> `docker-compose.yml` wiring app + Postgres + a one-shot migration)? Run
> `autumn release init --target docker-compose`. That is a separate,
> production-oriented stack — it overwrites the scaffold's `Dockerfile` and
> `.dockerignore` (pass `--force`, since `autumn new` already wrote them), so
> reach for it when you're packaging for deploy, not for the quick local DB above.

### 3. Apply migrations

```sh
autumn migrate
```

Applies every pending migration to the database you configured above. This
requires a resolved database URL — run step 2 first, or `autumn migrate` exits
with `✗ No database URL found.`

### 4. Run the dev server

```sh
autumn dev
```

Then visit **http://localhost:3000** — you should get a `200` with
"Welcome to {{project_name}}!". Health endpoints are auto-mounted at
`/health` and `/actuator/health`.

## CLI reference

The most useful `autumn` verbs for day-to-day work:

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `autumn dev` | Run the dev server with file watching + live reload. |
| `autumn migrate` | Apply pending database migrations. |
| `autumn doctor` | Preflight your environment / diagnose setup problems. |
| `autumn routes` | List all mounted routes. |
| `autumn generate scaffold <Name> field:Type …` | Scaffold a CRUD resource — model, migration, routes, and views. |
| `autumn release init --target docker-compose` | Generate deployment assets (e.g. a docker-compose with Postgres). |

## Project layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `autumn.toml` | Base config (server, database, session, security, logging). |
| `src/main.rs` | AppBuilder setup — register routes, tasks, jobs, migrations here. |
| `migrations/` | Diesel migrations — one directory per migration. |
| `static/` | Static assets served under `/static/`. |
